     * at least 1 byte to be in the pipe before our write.
     * Trick: use offset=1 for the splice then seek to the right place. */

    /* Actually the standard trick is: splice from (offset) bytes so
     * the page is loaded; then write goes into that page at offset%PAGE_SIZE */

    /* But if offset = 0, we need to be at the START of the page.
     * The flag PIPE_BUF_FLAG_CAN_MERGE merges if we write at a non-full page.
     * The standard exploit splices (offset) bytes from the start,
     * which puts us at position (offset % PAGE_SIZE) in the last page.
     * Then write merges at that position. */

